where \(x\) is the position operator and \(p\) is the momentum operator. This Hamiltonian is not Hermitian in the usual sense but can be made so by considering a suitable inner product. The spectrum of this Hamiltonian, if it exists, is conjectured to correspond to the imaginary parts of the non-trivial zeros of the Riemann zeta function.

